-a4c9870c9a10","timestamp":"2026-11-21T20:09:34.159Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/danie/quantum-icing-qoro","sessionId":"a6aa0d7e-04c8-4702-8eda-952590908d5e","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"main","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"b673e3b9-613f-49cf-af73-a4c9870c9a10","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fbd7c847-bb13-4c9d-8b3d-9d904e035a94","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ti78YpckXN2tRy5LEZCAVA","type":"tool_result","content":"- [Rispondi in italiano](rispondi-in-italiano.md) — the user wants every reply in Italian\n- [Strategia network design](strategia-network-design.md) — traccia scelta, target network24, domanda aperta ai mentor\n- [Macchina con RAM limitata](macchina-ram-limitata.md) — 7.4 GB di RAM: al massimo ~6 processi Python pesanti, con un controllo della memoria\n---\nname: macchina-ram-limitata\ndescription: \"La macchina WSL dell'utente ha 16 core ma solo 7.4 GB di RAM: troppi processi Python paralleli la bloccano\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 6f720823-c4f5-45f3-9607-b9b11e03bf37\n  modified: 2026-11-21T19:59:57.085Z\n---\n\nLa macchina (WSL) ha 16 core ma solo 7.4 GB di RAM e 2 GB di swap; Pylance da solo occupa 1–2 GB. Il 2026-11-21 circa 20 processi Python paralleli (4 subagent, ognuno con worker LP, Divi e simulatori) hanno esaurito RAM e swap: la macchina si è bloccata e WSL si è riavviato, cancellando anche lo scratchpad in /tmp.\n\n**Why:** l'utente ha dovuto segnalare il blocco e ha chiesto esplicitamente di non far bloccare tutto di nuovo.\n\n**How to apply:** non dimensionare il parallelismo sui core ma sulla RAM: tenere al massimo circa 6 processi Python pesanti insieme, controllare `free -m` prima di lanciare, e lanciare i run lunghi con un controllo che li ferma se MemAvailable scende sotto circa 1.2 GB. Salvare in modo duraturo (non in /tmp) i file che devono sopravvivere a un riavvio. Vedi [[strategia-network-design]].\n---\nname: rispondi-in-italiano\ndescription: The user wants every reply written in Italian\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 52b9d6f0-eee1-4f80-b1c0-e852b3f7b833\n  modified: 2026-11-21T10:58:48.107Z\n---\n\nAlways reply to the user in Italian (\"parlami sempre in italiano\", 2026-11-21).\n\n**Why:** Explicit standing request from the user.\n**How to apply:** Write all user-facing replies in Italian. Code, commands, commit messages and repo files keep their existing language (the repo README and notebooks are in English) unless the user asks otherwise.\n---\nname: strategia-network-design\ndescription: \"Hackathon Qoro (nov 2026): traccia scelta = network design, obiettivo network24 (BKV 663688); domanda aperta ai mentor su scala vs qualità\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: baa491bc-203d-427a-a1d9-f25fcc582a10\n  modified: 2026-11-21T11:13:38.143Z\n---\n\nDal 2026-11-21 la strategia è la traccia network design (QOBLIB 08): mettere al sicuro presto un network24.sol validato, poi passare l'hackathon a ridurne la congestione. Il progetto da presentare: Divi propone batch di modifiche alla topologia e il routing LP esatto decide quali tenere. Target pubblicato network24 = 663688 (più basso è meglio).\n\n**Why:** network24 ha un target pubblicato al massimo della sua scala (552 variabili); il portfolio arriva a ~36 000 variabili ma per le istanze da 200 e 400 asset non ci sono punteggi pubblicati.\n\n**How to apply:** prima di spostarsi sul portfolio, va chiarito con i mentor Qoro quanto pesa la scala rispetto alla qualità e come valutano le istanze senza riferimento. Se conta soprattutto la dimensione e quelle istanze sono ammesse, si passa al portfolio (ottimizzare finestre temporali sovrapposte tenendo fisse le posizioni circostanti). Pipeline: `network_pipeline.py` (verify / search / status), soluzioni salvate in `solutions/` (i *.sol sono in .gitignore). Vedi [[rispondi-in-italiano]].\ntotal 704\ndrwxr-xr-x  9 danie danie   4096 Nov 21 20:07 .\ndrwxr-x--- 15 danie danie   4096 Nov 21 21:05 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie     56 Nov 21 12:00 .env\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 danie danie   4096 Nov 21 18:49 .git\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie    116 Nov 21 11:36 .gitignore\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 danie danie   4096 Nov 21 11:49 .venv\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie  65407 Nov 21 13:03 00_main_qubo_101.ipynb\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie  54211 Nov 21 11:36 01_portfolio_optimisation.ipynb\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie  58835 Nov 21 15:02 02_network_design.ipynb\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie  11357 Nov 21 11:36 LICENSE\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie   8933 Nov 21 11:36 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 danie danie   4096 Nov 21 20:08 __pycache__\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 danie danie   4096 Nov 21 17:37 ai_context\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie   2976 Nov 21 15:02 network12.sol\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie 144150 Nov 21 16:55 network24_report.pdf\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie 143605 Nov 21 16:55 network24_report_eng.pdf\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie  21963 Nov 21 14:30 network_divi.py\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie  24373 Nov 21 15:07 network_ils.py\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie  12472 Nov 21 14:19 network_pipeline.py\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie  25320 Nov 21 20:07 network_pool.py\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie  13445 Nov 21 14:37 network_pt.py\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 danie danie   4096 Nov 21 12:09 qoblib_data\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie  38269 Nov 21 11:36 qoblib_tools.py\n-rw-r--r--  1 danie danie  14940 Nov 21 11:47 slides-recap.txt\ndrwxr-xr-x 14 danie danie   4096 Nov 21 20:20 solutions\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 danie danie   4096 Nov 21 16:49 solutions_best\nagent_divi\nagent_divi_oracle\nagent_ils\nagent_ils10\nagent_poolA\nagent_poolB\nagent_poolC\nagent_pt\nagent_pt8\nagent_q1\nagent_q2\nagent_q4\nlog.csv\nnetwork05.sol\nnetwork24.sol\n# AI context: how the network24 solution was found\n\nMaterial that is **not** elsewhere in the repo, collected so that someone (or their AI assistant) can\nfollow how `solutions_best/network24.sol` (score 657,121, 0.99% below QOBLIB's best known 663,688)\nwas found. Start with `../network24_report_eng.pdf`, then use this folder for detail.\n\n## transcripts/\n\nFull Claude Code transcripts (JSONL, one event per line: user messages, assistant messages,\ntool calls and their outputs). Snapshot taken on 2026-11-21 at about 17:10. The user's email address\nhas been replaced with `<email-redacted>`.\n\n| File | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `main_session.jsonl` | The main session: plan, `network_pipeline.py`, network05 check, first network24 submission, launching the subagents, follow-up runs, Rust checker verification, the PDF reports. Mostly in Italian. |\n| `subagents/agent-ac080c5cb56fef21b.jsonl` | Subagent **parallel tempering**: wrote `network_pt.py`, 684,455 → 673,253. |\n| `subagents/agent-a5097a40907d9b1e4.jsonl` | Subagent **ILS** (iterated local search): wrote `network_ils.py` (incremental HiGHS LP, deep step), 684,455 → 673,219. |\n| `subagents/agent-a3ba794d3cd6c2cf1.jsonl` | Subagent **Divi**: wrote `network_divi.py` (QAOA on 16 qubits as a proposer); no improvement, a measured negative result. |\n| `subagents/*.meta.json` | Metadata for each subagent (task description). |\n\nTip: these files are large. Search them for keywords (`banked`, `score`, `step`, `deep`), or\nextract only the `\"type\":\"assistant\"` text messages, rather than reading them whole.\n\n## logs/\n\n| Folder | Content |\n|---|---|\n| `parallel_tempering/` | stdout of `network_pt.py` runs. `r1`, `r2`: plain PT (no gains). `r3`, `r5`: guided proposals (684,455 → 673,253). `rA`, `rB`: A/B test of the smoothing term. `pt_r6.log`: 30-min continuation (→ 666,300). `pt_r7.log`: 20 min from 661,760 (→ **657,121**, the final solution). Each line: replica scores, Metropolis acceptance and swap rates per temperature. |\n| `ils_stdout/` | stdout of `network_ils.py` runs. `run1`–`run5` were affected by an LP-update bug (fixed before run6). `run6.out`: escape from 683,887 to 673,219. `ils_run8.out`: 670,621 → 661,760 (first result below the record). `ils_run9.out`: independently found the same 657,121 topology. The matching structured logs are in `../solutions/agent_ils/run*.log`. |\n\n## scripts/\n\n| File | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `make_report.py`, `make_report_eng.py` | Build the Italian and English PDF reports from `solutions/**/log.csv` (needs `reportlab`, `matplotlib`). Usage: `python make_report_eng.py <repo_dir> <out.pdf>`. |\n| `analyze.py` | Summarises the Divi experiment log `solutions/agent_divi/divi_run_divi_s1.jsonl` (sampler comparison table). |\n\n## divi_docs_context7.md\n\nDivi documentation snippets (install, QAOA, PCE, partitioning ensembles, pipelines, backends) copied\non 2026-11-21 from https://context7.com/qoroquantum/divi. They track Divi's `main` branch, while the\nrepo pins `qoro-divi==0.16.2`: check an API against the installed version before using it.\n\n## Verifying the solution yourself\n\nFrom the repo root:\n\n```bash\npython -c \"import qoblib_tools as qt; print(qt.check_network_solution('solutions_best/network24.sol', 24, qt.load_network_demand(24)))\"\n```\n\nExpected output: `(True, 657121, 'valid')`. It was also checked with QOBLIB's official Rust\nchecker (`08-network/check` in the QOBLIB repo), which returned `VALID`.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8c44304c-fcc2-483f-b39a-98400d7cb9ae","timestamp":"2026-11-21T20:09:34.921Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- [Rispondi in italiano](rispondi-in-italiano.md) — the user wants every reply in Italian\n- [Strategia network design](strategia-network-design.md) — traccia scelta, target network24, domanda aperta ai mentor\n- [Macchina con RAM limitata](macchina-ram-limitata.md) — 7.4 GB di RAM: al massimo ~6 processi Python pesanti, con un controllo della memoria\n---\nname: macchina-ram-limitata\ndescription: \"La macchina WSL dell'utente ha 16 core ma solo 7.4 GB di RAM: troppi processi Python paralleli la bloccano\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 6f720823-c4f5-45f3-9607-b9b11e03bf37\n  modified: 2026-11-21T19:59:57.085Z\n---\n\nLa macchina (WSL) ha 16 core ma solo 7.4 GB di RAM e 2 GB di swap; Pylance da solo occupa 1–2 GB. Il 2026-11-21 circa 20 processi Python paralleli (4 subagent, ognuno con worker LP, Divi e simul