{"parentUuid":"d79c01f1-2196-41cc-ac4a-71ff8e3e59c1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGmzgnEtb4aGXXJDm2Lc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VVe4Yfwv7YDPwdJNGZLdNv","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Quantum compound moves on network24","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are improving a QOBLIB 08 network-design solution for `network24` using a quantum sampler (Divi QAOA / PCE) inside a local search. HARD DEADLINES (wall clock, CET; check with `date`): your runs must be launched by 22:42 and must stop by 23:03 (wrap them in `timeout`); send your final report by 23:08. Do not exceed this.\n\n## Context (already measured, trust it)\n- Repo: /home/danie/quantum-icing-qoro. Activate: `source .venv/bin/activate`. Run Python with `PYTHONPATH=.:solutions/agent_qcompound`. Your working folder: /home/danie/quantum-icing-qoro/solutions/agent_qcompound/net24/ (create it). Do NOT read or use other `solutions/agent_*` folders (user's instruction: don't build on other sessions' work). You MAY import infrastructure from the repo root: `qoblib_tools` (as qt) and `network_ils.WarmLP`, `network_ils.move_2ex`.\n- Problem: 24 nodes, directed graph, every node out-degree 2 and in-degree 2, no self-loops, 48 arcs. Score = min over splittable multicommodity routing of the max arc load, ×1000, ceil (lower is better). Published best-known 663688. Our current best: `solutions_best/network24.sol`, score 657121 (LP z_lp 657120.97). Read with `_, arcs, _ = qt.read_network_solution(path)`.\n- Fast exact scorer: `W = WarmLP(D, arcs)`; `z, du = W.solve(arcs)` returns LP value and 48 arc dual prices; `basis = W.h.getBasis()`; then `W.solve(new_arcs, basis=basis)` ≈ 22 ms per neighbour (new_arcs must be a list of 48 arcs where slot positions correspond — `move_2ex(arcs, p, q)` returns such a list: arcs (a,b),(c,d) at slots p,q become (a,d),(c,b), or None if a self-loop). Also check `len(set(new))==48` (no duplicate arcs). `W.solve(new, cutoff=X, basis=basis)` returns (None, None) quickly if LP ≥ X. See solutions/agent_qcompound/probe1.py for a working example.\n- Landscape at 657121: 936 valid 2-exchanges, ALL worse; best Δ = +3110, then +4187, +4336, +4935, ... (sorted list saved in solutions/agent_qcompound/probe1_moves.npy as rows (z, p, q)). 25 of 48 arcs sit at max load; 23 arcs have positive dual price. It is a sharp local optimum for single moves, found independently by parallel tempering and ILS, so single moves, rot3 and node relabels are already exhausted. The bet is COMPOUND moves (several 2-exchanges applied at once), whose effect is not additive because the objective is a min-max: two moves that each relieve a different saturated arc are useless alone but can improve together.\n- Divi (qoro-divi 0.16.2) QAOA works locally: see solutions/agent_qcompound/qaoa_probe.py (20 qubits, p=2, MonteCarloOptimizer(population_size=20), max_iterations=5, MaestroSimulator(shots=4000): 101 circuits, 10.5 s, 495 MB RSS). `q.get_top_solutions(n=...)` returns SolutionEntry(bitstring, prob). VERIFY the bit order ↔ BQM variable mapping (e.g. compare bqm.energy of the decoded sample for a known state, or build bqm with integer variables 0..N-1 and check against `BinaryOptimizationProblem` docs/attributes). Notebook 02_network_design.ipynb cell 19 shows PCE usage: `PCE(BinaryOptimizationProblem(bqm), encoding=PolyEncoding(), objective=SoftObjective(alpha=2.0), n_layers=2, optimizer=MonteCarloOptimizer(population_size=..), max_iterations=.., backend=MaestroSimulator(...), seed=1)`, then `pce.get_top_solutions(n=100, min_prob=0.0, sort_by=\"energy\")`.\n\n## RAM (critical — the machine has 7.4 GB and froze before)\nAt most 2 heavy Python processes at the same time for you. Every long script must start with `import memguard; memguard.start(min_mb=900)` (module in solutions/agent_qcompound). Check `free -m` before launching. Never use multiprocessing pools.\n\n## Method to implement: Quantum Compound Moves (QCM)\nIterate until the time limit:\n1. Current topology T (start: the 657121 one), LP + basis. Evaluate all 2-exchanges → Δ_i = z_i − z0 (exact LP).\n2. Pick N candidate moves (low Δ, diversity: each arc slot used by at most 2 candidates so many candidates are mutually compatible; process B also favours moves that remove a positive-price arc, using `du`).\n3. Exact pair interactions: for every compatible pair (4 distinct slots, result valid, no duplicate arcs) LP the combined move: J_ij = z_ij − z0 − Δ_i − Δ_j. If any z_ij < best → accept immediately. Conflicting/invalid pairs get a penalty P (≈ 2× largest |coefficient|).\n4. QUBO over y ∈ {0,1}^N: E(y) = Σ Δ_i y_i + Σ J_ij y_i y_j + P·conflicts (normalised). This is the exact 2nd-order expansion of the true objective in move space; the quantum sampler searches the 2^N combinations (3–6 simultaneous moves), which pair enumeration cannot reach.\n5. Sample it with the quantum routine, decode, sort distinct conflict-free samples with ≥3 moves by QUBO energy, LP-evaluate the top K (≈30–50) exactly (apply moves sequentially on slot lists; check validity). Improvement (ceil score lower than best) → accept, bank, go to 1.\n6. No improvement → ILS kick: move to the best LP-evaluated compound if within +1.5% of the current, forbid re-adding just-removed arcs for a few iterations; every ~4 non-improving kicks restart from the best.\nRun TWO processes (different seeds): \n- Process A: QAOA, N=20 qubits, p=2–3, small MC budget (pop 20, 5 iters), shots 10000.\n- Process B: \"more qubits/variables\": PCE on a bigger pool N≈40–60 (PolyEncoding packs them on few qubits), optionally refit: after each round add the LP-evaluated combos as data and correct the QUBO (BOCS/FMQA-style ridge regression on singles+pairs features) before resampling.\nLog (to your folder) every iteration: z_current, best, #LPs, best QUBO energy found by the quantum sampler vs by dwave `SimulatedAnnealingSampler` on the same BQM (cheap, just energies), and the LP value of the best compound. This is for an honest quantum-vs-classical comparison.\n\n## Banking\nWhenever a topology scores below the current best (657121 at start), call `bank.bank(24, arcs, '<method description>', 'solutions/agent_qcompound/net24')` (module in solutions/agent_qcompound: integral routing + official checker + log.csv). Also print it. Never touch solutions_best/.\n\nFirst spend ≤10 minutes writing and smoke-testing (one iteration with small N) before launching the real runs. Keep it simple and correct rather than fancy.\n\n## Final report (concise, ≤250 words)\nBest score reached (and whether banked + checker result), path of the .sol, what each process did, how many compound moves were LP-evaluated, whether any improvement came from the quantum sampler vs from the exact pair step, QAOA/PCE vs SA energy comparison, script paths.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2478,"cache_read_input_tokens":103405,"output_tokens":5380,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":402},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2478,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5380,"cache_read_input_tokens":103405,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2478,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2478},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":27202,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VVe4Yfwv7YDPwdJNGZLdNv":{"description":"Quantum compound moves on network24","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are improving a QOBLIB 08 network-design solution for `network24` using a quantum s