 0 | 657,121 | 663,688 (best known) | −0.99% |\n\nThe `network05` and `network24` solutions were found by classical searches. `network18`–`network23` come from a hybrid chain, network23 → network18. Each instance starts from the polished topology of the next larger one with its last node deleted. Exact-LP 2-exchange descent refines it, and a QAOA step (Divi, local Maestro simulator, 18 qubits, p=2) samples combinations of 2-exchange moves to escape local optima. QAOA samples gave direct improvements on network22 and network19 and kicks before later descents on network20, while most of the gain came from the classical descent and the exact pair scan. The search code and logs are in [solutions/agent_qcompound/small/](../solutions/agent_qcompound/small/) (`qls.py`, `run_p1.log`, `log.csv`)."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"bbb55843-e3fa-4f9a-9ce0-28d0562d8802","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChGqjZXj1erMptMm2ZKZy","requestRef":"1823099a-838a-4c76-af54-519bccf37a4b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"bdc80423-618a-4e3d-9bc1-bbdabc2ec6d2","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:12:28.689Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/danie/quantum-icing-qoro/solutions/agent_qcompound/small","sessionId":"a6aa0d7e-04c8-4702-8eda-952590908d5e","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"main","dataFlowOn":true}
