es the heads of two to six arcs, preserving both degrees. A classical screen uses demand-weighted path lengths and excess link loads. The second stage refines that estimate using five weighted shortest-path routings and the current topology's routing LP duals. A threshold phase oracle marks roughly the best 12% of the resulting pool. Grover reflections on the uniform superposition amplify those indices. The simulator uses up to 11 index qubits, with 2,048 shots per round. Exact routing LPs score the measured topologies. Integer routing and the solution checker decide which records to keep. Bounded uphill steps let the search leave the radius-3 optima. [Implementation](../network_design/quantum_congestion.py)\n+\n+Greedy and uniform selection received the same routing budget of 120 distinct candidates per round from the same pool. The Grover-selected candidates alone determined the next search state. Over 364 rounds, Grover recorded 4 wins, 309 ties and 51 losses against greedy selection, and 294 wins, 56 ties and 14 losses against uniform selection. The comparison uses the best routing LP value per selector and treats two sets of candidates that both exceed the LP cutoff as a tie. Greedy matched the LP score of each new record on its winning round.\n+\n+The scores come from ideal statevector simulation with a classically precomputed phase oracle. A gate-level Qiskit simulation reproduced the probabilities of the first improving `network23` round within `1.3e-13`. Transpiling that 11-qubit circuit to `rz`, `sx`, `x` and `cx` yielded 17,164 CNOTs before hardware mapping.\n+\n+The following command reproduces 52 rounds per instance using the project virtual environment.\n+\n+```bash\n+for n in 18 19 20 21 22 23 24; do\n+  OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 .venv/bin/python -m network_design.quantum_congestion \\\n+    --nodes \"$n\" --seed 73 --rounds 52 --output-dir \"runs/network-grover/reproduce$n\"\n+done\n+```\n+\n+The command writes one JSONL comparison log per instance and saves checked improvements as `.sol` files. [Measured results](network_quantum/benchmark.csv) · [QOBLIB reference scores](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/blob/main/08-network/solutions/README.md)\n+\n ## Portfolio optimisation (QOBLIB 06)\n \n [portfolio/](portfolio/README.md) holds 221 checked `.sol` files, one per (instance, budget, λ). A **classical** search produced all of them (0 qubits): exact asset-trajectory DP, a day-level tabu search, ILS and parallel tempering, implemented in [portfolio_search.py](../portfolio_search.py). All 56 `po_a010` configurations and 34 of the 56 `po_a050` ones match QOBLIB's best-known value. Six `po_a050` configurations go below it, and 16 stay above it, mostly with λ = 1e-3 (gaps of 0.3–2.8%) and three with λ = 1e-2. The 109 `po_a200`/`po_a400` files (13 on the `_orig` instances, 96 on the 12 seed instances `s00`–`s02` with all 8 λ) have no published value to compare against.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a407311f-4317-4cff-844b-9e642ffa0af2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/danie/quantum-icing-qoro","root":"/home/danie/quantum-icing-qoro","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"LorenzoLaCorte/quantum-icing-qoro","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"LorenzoLaCorte/quantum-icing-qoro","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"LorenzoLaCorte/quantum-icing-qoro","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/danie/quantum-icing-qoro","platform":"wsl"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d58e3577-6bb6-40b5-b37a-a1b17c2c7330","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/danie/quantum-icing-qoro","sessionId":"a6aa0d7e-04c8-4702-8eda-952590908d5e","version":"2.1.330","gi